## =============================================================================
## SysML 1.7 → SysML 2.0 Migration Export Template  v6 (Diagram Edition)
## Tool:   CATIA Magic / MSOSA 2026x — Report Wizard (plain text output, .tsv)
## Output: Tab-Separated Values — 33 columns, one row per element
##
## v6.1 FIXES (2026-07-18) vs v6:
##   FIX-D  Metaclass-guarded every property read. The engine logs
##          "No such property: X of <metaclass>" WARNs whenever a template
##          reads a feature the metaclass lacks (.type/.lowerValue on
##          packages/blocks/relationships, .source/.target on Connectors,
##          .name/.qualifiedName on ConnectorEnds, .direction on ports,
##          .name on Comments/ProfileApplications at the model root,
##          .tag on ElementTaggedValues). Output was unaffected (reads
##          yielded empty) but the log was flooded; now reads only happen
##          on metaclasses that own the feature.
##
## v6 FIXES (2026-07-17) vs v5:
##   FIX-A  Removed every blank line / indented directive inside the ROW macro.
##          v5 emitted ~27 blank output lines PER ELEMENT (≈38,600 blank lines
##          for the HSUV model) plus stray space-only lines. Engine rule:
##          blank template lines and leading indentation LEAK into output.
##   FIX-B  Column 21 "Element ID" now carries the MagicDraw element ID
##          ($el.getID()) for EVERY element — it matches the Element ID column
##          of the CATIA migration report (MigrationReportOf<project>.xlsx),
##          enabling exact-ID matching in compare_migration.py. (v5 tried to
##          read the requirement Id tag here and always produced empty.)
##   FIX-C  Central sanitation of ALL 33 columns: tabs → space, line breaks →
##          the literal token <NL>. v5 left association-end names/QNs (cols
##          32-33) and dependency client/supplier lists unsanitized, so names
##          containing a real newline (e.g. 'WirelessTire\nPressureMonitor')
##          split a row into two corrupt lines. Consumers: treat <NL> as a
##          line break inside a name.
##
## HOW TO USE (no edits required):
##   1. Tools → Report Wizard → select this .vm file
##   2. Set scope to one of:
##        - A Package  → exports that package and all its descendants
##        - The Model  → exports all user packages (skips Cameo/SysML libs)
##        - (none)     → same as Model scope — full model with lib skip
##   3. Run and save output as .tsv
##   Works for ANY SysML 1.7 project — no hardcoded package names.
##
## COLUMNS 1-21 (same as base template):
##   1  Phase                         — migration phase 1-6
##   2  SysML 1.7 Element Type        — canonical type label
##   3  Name                          — element name
##   4  Owner Qualified Name          — owner's fully qualified name
##   5  Applied Stereotype            — Cameo humanType (stereotype-aware)
##   6  Qualified Name                — element's fully qualified name
##   7  Type Qualified Name           — type of property/port/pin
##   8  Multiplicity                  — lower..upper
##   9  Direction                     — in / out / inout (FlowProperty, Port, Param)
##  10  Source/Client QN              — connector source, dep client, flow source
##  11  Src End Part With Port QN     — Connector end-0 owning part
##  12  Target/Supplier QN            — connector target, dep supplier, flow target
##  13  Tgt End Part With Port QN     — Connector end-1 owning part
##  14  Item Conveyed QN              — ItemFlow conveyed type
##  15  Called Behavior QN            — CallBehaviorAction called behavior
##  16  Source Node QN                — ControlFlow/ObjectFlow/Transition source node
##  17  Target Node QN                — ControlFlow/ObjectFlow/Transition target node
##  18  Trigger                       — Transition trigger name(s)
##  19  Guard Expression              — Transition/edge guard
##  20  Signal QN                     — SignalEvent signal or Trigger event
##  21  Element ID                    — MagicDraw element ID ($el.getID()); matches
##                                      the CATIA migration report / mdzip XMI IDs
##
## DIAGRAM-SUPPORT COLUMNS 22-33:
##  22  Diagram Type                  — humanType for Diagram elements (BDD/IBD/STM/AD…)
##  23  General / Parent QN           — Generalization: parent classifier QN (BDD)
##  24  CE0 Role QN                   — Connector end-0 role property/port QN (IBD/Param)
##  25  CE1 Role QN                   — Connector end-1 role property/port QN (IBD/Param)
##  26  State Entry Behavior QN       — State entry behavior (STM)
##  27  State Exit Behavior QN        — State exit behavior (STM)
##  28  State Do Activity QN          — State do-activity (STM)
##  29  Transition Effect QN          — Transition effect behavior (STM)
##  30  Pseudostate Kind              — initial / choice / fork / join / etc. (STM)
##  31  Partition Represents QN       — ActivityPartition represented element (AD swim lane)
##  32  Association End 0             — role :: typeQN :: mult :: aggregation (BDD)
##  33  Association End 1             — role :: typeQN :: mult :: aggregation (BDD)
##
## ── KNOWN GAPS (human-in-the-loop required after import) ──────────────────
##  GAP-01  BindingConnector parameter-to-attribute mapping
##          CE0/CE1 Role QN give endpoint property QNs but the exact
##          bind <param> = <valueProperty> statement placement inside the
##          owning part def must be verified manually in MSOSA 2026.
##  GAP-02  Diagram visual layout and positioning
##          No x/y coordinates are exported. MSOSA will auto-layout all
##          regenerated diagrams. Human must manually reposition elements
##          to match original diagram layouts.
##  GAP-03  Activity diagram pin-to-port wiring
##          InputPin / OutputPin types are captured but their connections
##          to specific port flows on called behaviors are not resolvable
##          from element data alone; wiring must be recreated manually.
##  GAP-04  State machine history states and concurrent regions
##          Pseudostate Kind captures shallow/deep history, fork, join,
##          junction, choice, but concurrent (orthogonal) region ordering
##          and history state targets must be verified manually.
##  GAP-05  Requirement text body and Id tag
##          Requirement text and the SysML Id tagged value are not exported;
##          re-enter manually or import from the original source (Word,
##          ReqIF, etc.). (Column 21 is the MagicDraw element ID, not the
##          requirement Id tag.)
##  GAP-06  Matrix / table configuration
##          Dependency matrices and tables are MSOSA view configurations,
##          not model elements. They must be recreated manually in MSOSA
##          using the exported element lists and relationship rows.
##  GAP-07  Swimlane ordering within an Activity
##          ActivityPartition "represents" QN is captured (col 31) but
##          the left-to-right ordering of swim lanes must be set manually.
##  GAP-08  Diagram frame membership
##          Which elements appear inside a given IBD or BDD frame is not
##          exported. Auto-diagram in MSOSA uses element ownership to
##          populate frames; custom membership must be added manually.
##  GAP-09  Association navigability and ownership
##          Col 32-33 export role/type/mult/aggregation for each end but
##          the navigability arrows on BDD associations must be set
##          manually in the MSOSA diagram editor.
##  GAP-10  Connector association type linkage
##          Plain Connectors linking parts on IBDs reference an Association
##          type; this linkage is not captured and must be set manually.
##  GAP-11  Transition effect body (OpaqueBehavior)
##          Col 29 captures the effect behavior QN. If the effect is an
##          inline OpaqueBehavior (anonymous), the body text is lost and
##          must be re-entered manually.
##  GAP-12  Visual styling, colors, fonts, custom icons
##          All presentation properties are discarded. MSOSA default
##          styles will apply; custom styling must be reapplied manually.
##  GAP-13  Content / Context Diagram custom annotations
##          Free-text notes, callouts, and legend entries on context
##          diagrams (beyond LegendItem elements) are not captured.
##  GAP-14  Tagged values beyond Direction
##          Only the SysML direction tag is actively read. Custom tagged
##          values (e.g. rationale, source, priority, requirement Id/text)
##          must be exported separately or re-entered.
## =============================================================================
## ── METACLASSES TO SKIP (Cameo internals / noise) ───────────────────────────
#set($SKIP_MC = ["Slot","InstanceSpecification","ElementImport","PackageImport",
"TemplateSignature","TemplateBinding","TemplateParameterSubstitution",
"OpaqueExpression","LiteralInteger","LiteralUnlimitedNatural","LiteralString",
"LiteralBoolean","LiteralReal","LiteralNull","FunctionBehavior",
"InteractionConstraint","Duration","TimeExpression","Interval","TimeConstraint",
"ProfileApplication","BooleanTaggedValue","StringTaggedValue","IntegerTaggedValue",
"RealTaggedValue","EnumerationTaggedValue","TaggedValue","ElementTaggedValue",
"Stereotype","ExtensionEnd","Extension","Image","Comment"])
## ── METACLASSES THAT OWN A GIVEN FEATURE (guards against engine WARNs) ──────
## Only these metaclasses have .type:
#set($TYPED_MC = ["Property","Port","Parameter","InputPin","OutputPin",
"ActivityParameterNode","CentralBufferNode","DataStoreNode","ExtensionEnd"])
## Only these metaclasses have .lowerValue/.upperValue (MultiplicityElement):
#set($MULT_MC = ["Property","Port","Parameter","InputPin","OutputPin",
"ConnectorEnd","ExtensionEnd"])
## ── ROW MACRO ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
## Sets all 33 column variables then outputs ONE tab-separated line.
## Primary type discriminator: $el.humanType ($ht) — Cameo stereotype-aware name.
## NOTE: every line in this macro starts at column 0 and there are NO blank
## lines — the Report Wizard engine leaks indentation and blank lines into
## the output (once per element visited).
#macro(ROW $el)
#set($mc = $el.eClass().name)
#set($ht = $el.humanType)
## ── COL 1: Phase ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#if($ht == "Model" || $ht == "Package" || $mc == "Model" || $mc == "Package")#set($PH="1"
)#elseif($ht == "Signal" || $ht == "ValueType" || $ht == "Value Type" || $mc == "Signal" || $mc == "DataType")#set($PH="1"
)#elseif($ht == "InterfaceBlock" || $ht == "Interface Block" || $ht == "ConstraintBlock" || $ht == "Constraint Block")#set($PH="1"
)#elseif($mc == "Enumeration" || $mc == "EnumerationLiteral")#set($PH="1"
)#elseif($ht == "Block" || $ht == "Requirement" || $ht == "UseCase" || $ht == "Use Case" || $ht == "Actor")#set($PH="2"
)#elseif($ht == "TestCase" || $ht == "Test Case" || $ht == "Legend" || $mc == "Diagram")#set($PH="2"
)#elseif($mc == "Class" || $mc == "UseCase" || $mc == "Actor")#set($PH="2"
)#elseif($mc == "Generalization" || $mc == "Association")#set($PH="2"
)#elseif($ht == "Part Property" || $ht == "PartProperty" || $ht == "Value Property" || $ht == "ValueProperty")#set($PH="3"
)#elseif($ht == "Reference Property" || $ht == "ReferenceProperty" || $ht == "Flow Property" || $ht == "FlowProperty")#set($PH="3"
)#elseif($ht == "Constraint Property" || $ht == "ConstraintProperty" || $ht == "Proxy Port" || $ht == "ProxyPort")#set($PH="3"
)#elseif($ht == "Constraint Parameter" || $ht == "ConstraintParameter" || $mc == "Property" || $mc == "Port")#set($PH="3"
)#elseif($ht == "Binding Connector" || $ht == "BindingConnector" || $ht == "Item Flow" || $ht == "ItemFlow")#set($PH="4"
)#elseif($mc == "Connector" || $mc == "ConnectorEnd" || $mc == "InformationFlow")#set($PH="4"
)#elseif($mc == "StateMachine" || $mc == "Activity" || $mc == "State" || $mc == "Region" || $mc == "Pseudostate")#set($PH="5"
)#elseif($mc == "Transition" || $mc == "Trigger" || $mc == "SignalEvent" || $mc == "CallBehaviorAction" || $mc == "AcceptEventAction")#set($PH="5"
)#elseif($mc == "ControlFlow" || $mc == "ObjectFlow" || $mc == "ActivityFinalNode" || $mc == "InitialNode" || $mc == "ActivityParameterNode")#set($PH="5"
)#elseif($mc == "InputPin" || $mc == "OutputPin" || $mc == "Parameter" || $mc == "ActivityPartition")#set($PH="5"
)#elseif($ht == "Satisfy" || $ht == "Verify" || $ht == "Allocate" || $ht == "DeriveReqt" || $ht == "Derive Reqt")#set($PH="6"
)#elseif($mc == "Abstraction" || $mc == "Dependency" || $mc == "Constraint")#set($PH="6"
)#else#set($PH="0")#end
## ── COL 2: SysML 1.7 Element Type ────────────────────────────────────────────
#if($ht == "Model" || $mc == "Model")#set($ET="Model"
)#elseif($ht == "Package" || $mc == "Package")#set($ET="Package"
)#elseif($ht == "Signal" || $mc == "Signal")#set($ET="Signal"
)#elseif($ht == "UseCase" || $ht == "Use Case" || $mc == "UseCase")#set($ET="UseCase"
)#elseif($ht == "Actor" || $mc == "Actor")#set($ET="Actor"
)#elseif($mc == "Generalization")#set($ET="Generalization"
)#elseif($ht == "Association" || $mc == "Association")#set($ET="Association"
)#elseif($mc == "Enumeration")#set($ET="Enumeration"
)#elseif($mc == "EnumerationLiteral")#set($ET="EnumerationLiteral"
)#elseif($mc == "Diagram")#set($ET="Diagram"
)#elseif($mc == "StateMachine")#set($ET="StateMachine"
)#elseif($mc == "Activity")#set($ET="Activity"
)#elseif($mc == "State")#set($ET="State"
)#elseif($mc == "Region")#set($ET="Region"
)#elseif($mc == "Pseudostate")#set($ET="Pseudostate"
)#elseif($mc == "Transition")#set($ET="Transition"
)#elseif($mc == "Trigger")#set($ET="Trigger"
)#elseif($mc == "SignalEvent")#set($ET="SignalEvent"
)#elseif($mc == "ControlFlow")#set($ET="ControlFlow"
)#elseif($mc == "ObjectFlow")#set($ET="ObjectFlow"
)#elseif($mc == "ActivityFinalNode")#set($ET="ActivityFinalNode"
)#elseif($mc == "InitialNode")#set($ET="InitialNode"
)#elseif($mc == "ActivityParameterNode")#set($ET="ActivityParameterNode"
)#elseif($mc == "CallBehaviorAction")#set($ET="CallBehaviorAction"
)#elseif($mc == "AcceptEventAction")#set($ET="AcceptEventAction"
)#elseif($mc == "InputPin")#set($ET="InputPin"
)#elseif($mc == "OutputPin")#set($ET="OutputPin"
)#elseif($mc == "Parameter")#set($ET="Parameter"
)#elseif($mc == "ConnectorEnd")#set($ET="ConnectorEnd"
)#elseif($ht == "Block")#set($ET="Block [Class]"
)#elseif($ht == "ConstraintBlock" || $ht == "Constraint Block")#set($ET="ConstraintBlock [Class]"
)#elseif($ht == "InterfaceBlock" || $ht == "Interface Block")#set($ET="InterfaceBlock [Class]"
)#elseif($ht == "Requirement")#set($ET="Requirement [Class]"
)#elseif($ht == "TestCase" || $ht == "Test Case")#set($ET="TestCase [Behavior, Operation]"
)#elseif($ht == "Legend")#set($ET="Legend [Class]"
)#elseif($ht == "ValueType" || $ht == "Value Type")#set($ET="ValueType [DataType]"
)#elseif($ht == "PartProperty" || $ht == "Part Property")#set($ET="PartProperty [Property]"
)#elseif($ht == "ValueProperty" || $ht == "Value Property")#set($ET="ValueProperty [Property]"
)#elseif($ht == "ReferenceProperty" || $ht == "Reference Property")#set($ET="ReferenceProperty [Property]"
)#elseif($ht == "FlowProperty" || $ht == "Flow Property")#set($ET="FlowProperty [Property]"
)#elseif($ht == "ConstraintProperty" || $ht == "Constraint Property")#set($ET="ConstraintProperty [Property]"
)#elseif($ht == "ProxyPort" || $ht == "Proxy Port")#set($ET="ProxyPort [Port]"
)#elseif($ht == "ConstraintParameter" || $ht == "Constraint Parameter")#set($ET="ConstraintParameter [Port]"
)#elseif($ht == "BindingConnector" || $ht == "Binding Connector")#set($ET="BindingConnector [Connector]"
)#elseif($ht == "ItemFlow" || $ht == "Item Flow" || $mc == "InformationFlow")#set($ET="ItemFlow [InformationFlow]"
)#elseif($ht == "Allocate")#set($ET="Allocate [Abstraction]"
)#elseif($ht == "Satisfy")#set($ET="Satisfy [Abstraction]"
)#elseif($ht == "Verify")#set($ET="Verify [Abstraction]"
)#elseif($ht == "DeriveReqt" || $ht == "Derive Reqt" || $ht == "Derive Requirement")#set($ET="DeriveReqt [Abstraction]"
)#elseif($mc == "Abstraction")#set($ET="Abstraction"
)#elseif($mc == "Dependency")#set($ET="Dependency"
)#elseif($ht == "LegendItem" || $ht == "Legend Item")#set($ET="LegendItem [Constraint]"
)#elseif($mc == "Constraint")#set($ET="Constraint"
)#elseif($ht == "AllocateActivityPartition" || $ht == "Allocate Activity Partition")#set($ET="AllocateActivityPartition [ActivityPartition]"
)#elseif($mc == "ActivityPartition")#set($ET="ActivityPartition"
)#elseif($mc == "Class")#set($ET="Class"
)#elseif($mc == "DataType")#set($ET="DataType"
)#elseif($mc == "Property")#set($ET="Property"
)#elseif($mc == "Port")#set($ET="Port"
)#elseif($mc == "Connector")#set($ET="Connector"
)#else#set($ET=$ht)#end
## ── COL 3–6: Name, Owner QN, humanType (stereotype), Qualified Name ──────────
## (raw values here; ALL columns are sanitized centrally just before output)
## ConnectorEnd has neither name nor qualifiedName - reading them WARNs.
#set($NM="")
#set($QN="")
#if($mc != "ConnectorEnd")
#if($el.name)#set($NM=$el.name)#end
#if($el.qualifiedName)#set($QN=$el.qualifiedName)#end
#end
#if($el.owner && $el.owner.qualifiedName)#set($OWN=$el.owner.qualifiedName)#else#set($OWN="")#end
#set($ST=$ht)
## ── COL 7: Type Qualified Name (only metaclasses that own .type) ─────────────
#set($TQN="")
#if($TYPED_MC.contains($mc) && $el.type && $el.type.qualifiedName)#set($TQN=$el.type.qualifiedName)#end
## ── COL 8: Multiplicity (only MultiplicityElement metaclasses) ───────────────
#set($MULT="")
#if($MULT_MC.contains($mc) && $el.lowerValue && $el.upperValue)#set($MULT="$el.lowerValue.value..$el.upperValue.value")#end
## ── COL 9: Direction (FlowProperty, ProxyPort, ConstraintParameter, Parameter)
## Only Parameter has a .direction feature; ports/properties carry it as a
## SysML tagged value. ElementTaggedValue lacks .tag - skip it in the loop.
#set($DIR="")
#if($mc == "Parameter" && $el.direction)#set($DIR=$el.direction.name)#end
#if($DIR == "" && ($ht == "FlowProperty" || $ht == "Flow Property" || $ht == "ProxyPort" || $ht == "Proxy Port" || $ht == "ConstraintParameter" || $ht == "Constraint Parameter"))
#foreach($tv in $el.taggedValue)
#if($tv.eClass().name != "ElementTaggedValue")
#if($tv.tag.name == "direction" || $tv.tag.name == "flowDirection" || $tv.tag.name == "Direction")
#if($DIR == "" && $tv.value)#set($DIR=$tv.value.name)#end
#end
#end
#end
#end
## ── COL 10: Source / Client QN ───────────────────────────────────────────────
## (Connector/BindingConnector have NO source/target - endpoints are exported
##  via cols 11/13 and 24/25 instead)
#set($SRC="")
#if($mc == "ControlFlow" || $mc == "ObjectFlow" || $mc == "Transition")
#if($el.source && $el.source.qualifiedName)#set($SRC=$el.source.qualifiedName)#end
#elseif($mc == "Abstraction" || $mc == "Dependency" || $mc == "Generalization")
